WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:03.670
Trust

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.180
Hey, hey.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.550
Apparently they have
good squid ink paella there.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.720
We should go sometime.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.660
No way, we can't eat here.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.560
You never know who could see us.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.570
Come on.
Walk ahead of me a little more.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.540
Okay, okay.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.750
Man, she has short legs.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.330
Great Passage

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:07.700
A quiet dreamlike morning, the madder red sky
shines through the window and reflects on my pen

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:13.840
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:20.480
Deep thoughts, flexible conception;
foreseeable aspirations, distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:27.120
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:33.430
The light in our eyes that differ from each other,
traces of friendship that’s not in the treaty

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:39.730
In the ocean that sweeps the sand of eternity

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.710
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:53.210
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:59.750
Reference, conclusion; I’ll gather words that have
scattered over many months and years

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:06.230
The fragrant sea breeze;
the connection that rests on the seashore, become one.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.540
Sensei, we appreciate
your continued contribution.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.650
Yes. Of course. Yes.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.520
Well, have a good day.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:34.850
What's the matter, Majime?

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.320
Lately I've been having difficulty
grasping things.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.860
Seriously? You've
lost your fingerprints already?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.800
And I've been here five years.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.400
I still have mine.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.500
It's hard to flip the pages.
It's very inconvenient.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.270
Hey, you'll be able to rob a bank
without gloves on now.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.310
Well, well. That's quite a disturbing
conversation you're having.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.610
Hey, you're the same too.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.950
-Nishioka, it's here.
-Yes, finally.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.850
Thank you very much.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.700
It seems like this manuscript
will require some significant work.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.370
I thought so.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:31.580
And so many are over the set character
limit. What about the writing guideline?

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.450
Of course I give him a copy.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.720
But it seems like he didn't read it.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.820
-Has he been informed about revisions?
-Yes, I've let him know.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.790
But this Oda-sensei is really touchy.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:49.400
I guess I'll cover my bases,
and let him know what we'll be changing.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.630
What about this entry on Saigyō?

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:56.000
To start with, I think there are
a lot of unnecessary words.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:01.540
Yeah. He has a lot of
his own personal opinions in here.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:05.850
"Every Japanese person will be moved
by Saigyō's poems."

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.720
We should not be using definitive words
like "every person."

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.990
Also this part about entering
the priesthood for his reasons.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.720
-I don't know where to start.
-Yes.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.560
There are varying opinions on
why Saigyō joined the priesthood.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:24.930
This section is far too vague,
so let's lose it all.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.670
Do we need this tanka poem here?

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.640
I believe we'll need to examine it
more closely later.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.010
But we could probably eliminate it
at this stage.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.880
It's finally coming together.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.990
Although I'm not sure
just an explanation of the person...

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.320
...for Saigyō's entry
is sufficient for the dictionary.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.560
-Does it have another meaning?
-Yes.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.330
From Saigyō's travels around Japan,

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:02.540
we sometimes refer to wanderers
or people who travel around as Saigyō.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.670
-Also...
-There's more?

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:10.080
Yes. There is a Noh play called
Saigyō-zakura.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.680
Wearing a conical hat with
crossed strings is called Saigyō-Kazuki.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:18.050
Also, wearing a cloth diagonally
is called Saigyō-Jyoi.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.990
Whoa, do you have multiple dictionaries
memorized or something?

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.730
I wish I could.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:30.100
In any case, it doesn't seem like
there's enough room to list them all.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:35.670
What definition do you think we should
include in Daitokai, Nishioka-san?

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.700
Let me think.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.410
If I have to choose, I would say
the wanderer or person who travels.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.010
-Why is that?
-Well...

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:50.880
The other meanings,
you can kind of imagine from context.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.820
I see, but...

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.590
For example...

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:59.130
Let's say a real world wanderer
looked over a dictionary.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.760
And in the entry for Saigyō,

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:05.570
they found out that it also means
wanderers or people who travel,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.100
because of Saigyō's travels,
they might think,

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:13.940
"Oh, there were people just like me
back then who couldn't stay in one place."

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:16.380
They might feel
pretty encouraged about that.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.750
What is it?

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:24.520
I have never thought of it that way.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:30.560
I mean, it might be wrong
from a dictionary's standpoint.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.160
No, I wouldn't say that.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:37.030
Sensei, are you okay on time?

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.770
Oh, thank you.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:42.570
-Nishioka, Majime.
-Yes?

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.840
You two make such a fantastic team.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:52.680
You respect each other's strengths
and complement each other.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.950
It's a wonderful trust you have.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.990
Well, please, excuse me.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.890
-Have a good night.
-Have a good night.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.630
Good Lord, it's chilly out here.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.560
I should've worn a jacket.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.200
Nishioka-san.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:20.140
I think it's very unfortunate
that you will be transferring.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:26.580
In order to make Daitokai a warm
and understanding dictionary,

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.950
I know that you're absolutely necessary.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.460
Majime.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.960
I might be transferring away soon,

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:45.200
but I'm proud of the work I did
on Daitokai with you.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:48.730
But this doesn't mean the end.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.110
No matter how far we're separated,

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:57.610
no matter the obstacles,

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:01.080
I'll be there to support you.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:04.020
Besides, there's still Matsumoto-sensei,

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.550
and everyone
at the Dictionary Department.

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:11.920
So even when you're by yourself,
you're not alone.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.700
Thank you very much.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.100
Let us do everything in our power

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.740
to complete Daitokai.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.850
Yeah.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:41.290
To Professor Oda

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:42.020
Sending...

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.790
Whoa, you're heading home already?
That's rare.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:54.100
Yes. Kaguya-san will be in charge
of her first dish at Ume no Mi tonight.

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:57.040
Would you like to come as well?

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.140
Oh, I know you'd rather go alone.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:03.910
Besides, I still have stuff to do.
I'll pass this time.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.550
-I see.
-Go on, get out of here.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.250
Okay. Have a nice night.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.550
Have fun.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.930
Note: Professor Oda
tends to ignore our style sheets.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:24.030
Internal use only

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:28.870
Let's see. Oda-sensei...

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:33.040
All right.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.650
Dear Kaguya

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.320
Whoa, he has a girlfriend?

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.060
Oh, I didn't mention it before?

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:58.630
Nope. I wonder if it's his first girlfriend.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:02.340
Yeah. He can finally
say goodbye to his virginity.

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:05.640
Well, that's nice for him.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.170
So, what's his girlfriend like?

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:13.750
She's really got everything together,
and super beautiful.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.890
I think I'll go take a bath.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:35.870
A dictionary is a ship to navigate
through a sea of words, huh?

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:42.910
Even when we're separated,
my feelings are the same.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:54.890
You sure took a long bath.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:59.260
Ugly as always.

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:11.040
You've been coming home late
these days.

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:15.040
I've got a lot to do
with my transfer coming up.

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:18.040
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.980
Good morning.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:27.920
Good morning.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:30.760
My eyes have been so itchy.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:34.930
Oh, that's right. You have allergies.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:38.330
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.870
Oh, Araki-san, your eyes are red.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:47.370
With all these talks of allergies, I definitely
feel that spring is just around the corner.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:49.180
It is March already.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.180
Which means we're down
to our last month with Nishioka.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:56.880
Hey, don't make it sound like I'm dying.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.790
Our PR Department is a real hell.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:06.860
I know so many people get abused
by our PR Department and quit.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:10.960
-Nishioka, don't die on me.
-Hold on.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:14.970
Don't scare me like that
with those red eyes of yours.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.740
-Sorry.
-Come on.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:21.370
Don't "achoo" me.

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:28.250
Yes, this is Genbu Books Publishing's
Dictionary Editorial Department.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:33.290
Yes, please, hold.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:37.960
Nishioka, it's Oda-sensei
from Kobun University.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.290
Okay, thank you.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.030
Hello, sensei. This is Nishioka.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.340
What is the meaning of this,
Nishioka-san?!

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:56.990
Yes. Understood. We will be in contact.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.760
Yes. Please, excuse me.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:04.430
-I need to go out for a moment.
-Is something wrong?

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:07.100
No, it's not a big deal.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.970
I'm sure knowing him,
he just wants someone to talk to.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:16.840
-Oh, all right.
-I'm off, then.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.520
This is Nishioka
from Genbu Books Publishing.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:24.850
Please, excuse me.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.820
-Sensei, I--
-Like I said earlier,

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.290
this is the first time I've had
my manuscript revised so much.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.130
-I am very sor--
-Never in my life.

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:37.930
I am terribly sorry.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:42.140
But a dictionary needs
a unified standard.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.840
Please, we would appreciate
your blessing.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:48.910
Were you the one
who wrote those revisions?

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:53.850
No, I brought it to the attention of
one of our editors named Majime.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:58.120
Really?
Oh, I've also heard, Nishioka-san.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:02.560
I understand you're being transferred.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:07.960
I was planning on informing you
about that in the near future.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.330
I will be transferring
at the end of the month.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:16.440
I don't want someone who would abandon
our work fiddling with my manuscript.

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:18.540
I have no intention
of abandoning anything.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.510
Sensei, it is true
that I will be transferring,

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:26.510
but Majime will be working with you
from now on.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.080
Majime is a man who can be trusted.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:37.260
Then this Majime-san can
write all the manuscripts himself.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.860
I will be washing my hands of this.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:51.170
Well, Majime and I are
very appreciative of your work.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:52.610
Well, that's...

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:56.280
Yes, I shouldn't be telling you this,

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:00.950
but other writers require even more
revision work on our end.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:05.320
Thanks to your manuscript,

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:07.950
we only had to adjust
to fit the standard guideline.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.520
Sensei, thank you so much
for your work.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.860
-I see.
-Yes.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.200
Well, I am willing
to accept these revisions,

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.430
seeing your display of apology here.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.370
Thank you very much.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.400
Although, it's not quite kneeling.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.640
Kneeling, sir?

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:41.290
I see. I understand.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:11.250
Daitokai has more pride than that.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:16.160
Sensei, that is a very good joke.

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:17.920
What are you talking about?

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:22.030
Let's suppose that you have a mistress.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.430
This is all hypothetical.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:29.170
But I would never use that to force you
to accept these revisions.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:33.240
Because I hate the idea
of testing people like that.

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:38.510
We both understand
what character and integrity are.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:43.350
Nishioka-san, are you transferring
to the tabloids,

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.620
and writing about celebrity affairs?

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:51.520
You can keep
your meaningless metaphors!

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:57.230
Such a good cook for being so young.

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:00.400
And I also hear
her grades are quite stellar.

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:02.970
-Why, you--
-Such a worthy recipient

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:05.140
of your personal guidance.

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:10.010
I hope that
we understand each other now.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:15.450
Thank you very much.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.330
Sensei.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.030
Our Daitokai's editorial team's resolve

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:38.070
is harder than the Earth's core,
and hotter than magma.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.310
Majime will create a dictionary
that will be trusted and loved

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:44.310
for many years to come.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:45.640
So...

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:51.150
We look forward
to your continued support.

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:59.660
Yes, this is Genbu Books Publishing's
Dictionary Editorial Department.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:04.360
-That you, Majime?
-Oh, Nishioka-san. How is Oda-sensei?

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.170
No problem at all.
We'll go with your manuscript.

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.400
I see. I'm glad to hear that.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:12.170
You don't seem that surprised.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:17.110
Knowing you, I had a feeling
it would all work out.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.040
Oh, right. I see.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:22.520
You are a man we can all rely on.

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:25.750
Oh, yes. That relying on each other
you spoke of.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:27.090
Yes.

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:33.090
Well, that's all
I wanted to tell you. Later.

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:52.310
To: Remi Miyoshi
You free tonight?

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:56.320
Let's go eat
that squid ink paella you mentioned.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.450
Sending

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:12.800
I'm free, but we might
run into someone from work.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:15.530
Who cares!
See you at the restaurant at 7!

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:22.210
Okay. I will try not to be late.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:25.850
All right!

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:44.800
To do list by the end of March

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:54.510
Even when you're by yourself,
you're not alone.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.690
Trust

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.490
All right.

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:25.640
Trust: To believe in each other
with respect

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:40.390
Hey, it’s a full moon tonight

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:51.400
I speak to you softly as you sleep

00:20:52.770 --> 00:21:03.240
Your gestures, attitude, and way of life

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:09.950
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:15.790
So please stay the way you are

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:21.890
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:27.370
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:40.280
I’ve loved you from the day we met

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:52.490
You need more gravitas. A pair of glasses
can change everything.

00:21:52.630 --> 00:21:55.490
I'll come help you pick out
the perfect pair of new glasses.

00:21:55.630 --> 00:21:56.700
No, this isn't it.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:00.000
Do you have any more snappy?
Oh, I like that.

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:03.740
-What about this? Whoa, that's snappy!
-I want to go home.
